---
import ArticleLayout from "@layouts/ArticleLayout.astro";
---

<ArticleLayout
  title="Suzuki Dealerships"
  description="A co-branded website network for Suzuki motorcycle dealerships, sharing brand content while each dealer promotes its own offers, stock and opening hours."
  eyebrow="Selected work / Website"
  subtitle="One brand voice, every dealership."
  tags="Web design · Development · Multi-site"
  backHref="/work/"
  backText="← Back to selected work"
>
  <figure slot="art" class="article-cover">
    <img
      src="/assets/suzuki/cover.jpg"
      alt="The Suzuki dealer home page with the all-new Hayabusa campaign and a single feature motorcycle"
      width="1440"
      height="900"
      fetchpriority="high"
    />
  </figure>

  <section>
    <h2>A website for every dealership.</h2>
    <p class="lead">
      Suzuki has more than a hundred motorcycle dealerships across Australia.
      Each one needs a website that carries the national brand, but speaks for
      the shop on the corner: its stock, its offers, its opening hours.
    </p>
    <p>
      The answer was a dealer microsite built on the content and components of
      the main Suzuki Motorcycles site. Campaigns, range pages and brand
      photography come from the parent site; the dealer adds what is local.
    </p>
    <a
      class="text-link"
      href="https://suzukimotorcycles.com.au/"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer"
    >
      Visit Suzuki Motorcycles ↗
    </a>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Shared content, local voice.</h2>
    <p>
      A campaign launched nationally appears on every dealer site without anyone
      at the dealership touching it. The feed keeps the network current and
      consistent, so no shop is left showing last season’s offer.
    </p>
    <p>
      On top of that shared layer, each dealer manages its own offers, new and
      certified used stock, services, social media and about information. The
      site is co-branded: clearly Suzuki, clearly that dealership.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Find a bike.</h2>
    <p>
      Buying locally means knowing what is actually on the floor. The Find A
      Bike module puts the dealer’s stock beside its details and opening hours,
      so a customer can move from the national range to a bike they can visit.
    </p>
    <p>
      It was also the hardest part to get right. A stock module that works for
      one shop has to work identically for every shop, with content the dealer
      can maintain. That decision shaped the rest of the template.
    </p>
    <figure>
      <a
        href="/assets/suzuki/dealer.jpg"
        aria-label="Open the full-size dealer page capture"
      >
        <img
          src="/assets/suzuki/dealer-web.jpg"
          alt="A Suzuki dealer page: dealer details and services above a local map, followed by offers, new stock and certified used bikes"
          width="1440"
          height="3190"
          loading="lazy"
        />
      </a>
      <figcaption>
        Dealer details, services and the local map above current offers and
        stock. Open the full capture ↗
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Five first, then the network.</h2>
    <p>
      With over a hundred sites to deliver, the planning came before the
      building. Together with Suzuki, the team went through the main site and
      decided which components would carry through, which content would be
      locked, and which parts the dealer could edit.
    </p>
    <p>
      One version of the dealer website was built, then five dealerships
      received it to customise and test. Their feedback came from the people who
      would use the site every day, so the template that went to the rest of the
      network had already been tested in a showroom rather than in theory.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>The template, up close.</h2>
    <p>
      The same structure carries across the home page, the range and the bike
      builder. Photography stays large, the routes stay plain, and the dealer
      content sits below the national story.
    </p>
    <div class="shot-pair">
      <figure>
        <a
          href="/assets/suzuki/home-desktop.jpg"
          aria-label="Open the full-size desktop home page capture"
        >
          <img
            src="/assets/suzuki/home-desktop-web.jpg"
            alt="The full desktop home page: Hayabusa campaign, featured motorcycles, road, off-road and ATV ranges, finance and services, news and dealer locator"
            width="1440"
            height="5000"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </a>
        <figcaption>Home page · Desktop · Open full size ↗</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="mobile-shot">
        <a
          href="/assets/suzuki/home-mobile.jpg"
          aria-label="Open the full-size mobile home page capture"
        >
          <img
            src="/assets/suzuki/home-mobile-web.jpg"
            alt="The mobile home page with the all-new Hayabusa campaign filling the first screen"
            width="750"
            height="1334"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </a>
        <figcaption>Home page · Mobile · Open full size ↗</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
    <figure>
      <a
        href="/assets/suzuki/bike-hayabusa.jpg"
        aria-label="Open the full-size Hayabusa page capture"
      >
        <img
          src="/assets/suzuki/bike-hayabusa-web.jpg"
          alt="The Hayabusa model page: hero photography, model history, colour and specification detail, finance, related models and dealer stock"
          width="1440"
          height="4470"
          loading="lazy"
        />
      </a>
      <figcaption>
        A single motorcycle: the range story, specifications, colours and the
        dealer’s stock. Open the full capture ↗
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure>
      <a
        href="/assets/suzuki/build-your-bike.jpg"
        aria-label="Open the full-size build your bike capture"
      >
        <img
          src="/assets/suzuki/build-your-bike-web.jpg"
          alt="The build your bike screen with racing kits, individual parts and accessories, each with a price and a select action"
          width="1440"
          height="2914"
          loading="lazy"
        />
      </a>
      <figcaption>
        Build your bike: kits, parts and accessories, with the price building as
        the choices are made. Open the full capture ↗
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure class="news-shot">
      <a
        href="/assets/suzuki/news-article.jpg"
        aria-label="Open the full-size news article capture"
      >
        <img
          src="/assets/suzuki/news-article-web.jpg"
          alt="A Suzuki news article on a narrow screen, with campaign photography, body copy and related articles"
          width="750"
          height="2400"
          loading="lazy"
        />
      </a>
      <figcaption>
        News and campaigns keep the same type and image rhythm on a narrow
        screen. Open the full capture ↗
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <aside class="project-status">
    Live network · Screens are supplied captures of the dealer template. Content
    belongs to individual dealerships and may change.
  </aside>
  <a class="text-link" href="/work/">
    Explore more selected work ↗
  </a>
</ArticleLayout>

<style>
  .shot-pair {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 3fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    align-items: start;
    gap: 20px;
    margin-top: 32px;
  }
  .shot-pair figure {
    min-width: 0;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .news-shot {
    width: min(100%, 360px);
    margin-inline: auto;
  }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .shot-pair {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 28px;
    }
    .shot-pair .mobile-shot {
      width: min(100%, 260px);
      justify-self: center;
    }
  }
</style>
